Chapter: Goose
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 IEC 61850 GOOSE (Generic Object Oriented Substation Event), the fast
 layer-2 multicast that carries protection and control signals between
 substation intelligent electronic devices in milliseconds -- the
 real-time complement to the DNP3 and IEC 104 SCADA telemetry. A GOOSE
 Ethernet frame carries EtherType 0x88B8, an eight-octet link header
 (APPID, length, two reserved fields), and an ASN.1 BER goosePdu whose
 context-tagged fields describe the control block, dataset, sequence
 counters, and the published data values. Lengths use the BER short
 form; integers use minimal big-endian encoding with a leading zero
 octet when the top bit would otherwise read as negative. Each builder
 returns a List Integer.

Section: BER Helpers

  goose-u16-be : Integer -> List Integer
  goose-u16-be (v) = [bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

  goose-tlv : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-tlv (tag) (val) = [tag, list-length val] & val

  goose-text-bytes : Text, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-text-bytes (s) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else goose-text-bytes s (i + 1) len (list-push acc (to-unicode (char-code (char-at s i))))

  goose-vstr : Integer, Text -> List Integer
  goose-vstr (tag) (s) = goose-tlv tag (goose-text-bytes s 0 (text-length s) [])

  goose-uint-bytes : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-uint-bytes (v) (acc) =
   if v <= 0 then acc else goose-uint-bytes (bit-shru v 8) ([bit-and v 255] & acc)

  goose-uint-fix : List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-uint-fix (raw) = if bit-and (list-at raw 0) #80 == 0 then raw else [0] & raw

  goose-uint-content : Integer -> List Integer
  goose-uint-content (v) = if v == 0 then [0] else goose-uint-fix (goose-uint-bytes v [])

  goose-integer : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  goose-integer (tag) (v) = goose-tlv tag (goose-uint-content v)

  goose-boolean : Integer, Boolean -> List Integer
  goose-boolean (tag) (b) = goose-tlv tag (if b then [#FF] else [#00])

  goose-octets : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-octets (tag) (bs) = goose-tlv tag bs

Section: Data Values

 Inside allData each value is a context-tagged MMS Data choice; a
 boolean is tag 0x83 with an all-ones or zero octet.

  goose-data-boolean : Boolean -> List Integer
  goose-data-boolean (b) = goose-tlv #83 (if b then [#FF] else [#00])

Section: GOOSE PDU

 The goosePdu is an APPLICATION 1 (0x61) sequence: the control-block
 reference, the hold time, the dataset and GOOSE id, the publish
 timestamp, the state and sequence numbers, the test and needs-commission
 flags, the configuration revision, the dataset entry count, and the
 data values (context tag 0x0B, encoded 0xAB).

  goose-pdu : Text, Integer, Text, Text, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer, Boolean, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-pdu (gocbref) (tal) (datset) (goid) (t8) (stnum) (sqnum) (test) (confrev) (ndscom) (numentries) (alldata) =
   let body = goose-vstr #80 gocbref & goose-integer #81 tal & goose-vstr #82 datset & goose-vstr #83 goid & goose-octets #84 t8 & goose-integer #85 stnum & goose-integer #86 sqnum & goose-boolean #87 test & goose-integer #88 confrev & goose-boolean #89 ndscom & goose-integer #8A numentries & goose-tlv #AB alldata
   in goose-tlv #61 body

Section: Frame

 The link header prefixes the goosePdu with the application identifier
 and a length covering the eight-octet header plus the PDU. The Ethernet
 frame prepends the destination and source addresses and EtherType 0x88B8.

  goose-header : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-header (appid) (pdu) =
   goose-u16-be appid & goose-u16-be (8 + list-length pdu) & goose-u16-be 0 & goose-u16-be 0 & pdu

  goose-eth-frame : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  goose-eth-frame (dst) (src) (appid) (pdu) =
   dst & src & [#88, #B8] & goose-header appid pdu
